    "title": "Texas men's basketball kicks off Sweet 16 against Purdue: Odds, TV",
    "text": "After becoming the only team in the NCAA tournament to win three games on opening week, No. 11 Texas looks to continue its Cinderella run when it takes on No. 2 Purdue in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA tournament.Purdue charged into the NCAA tournament by winning the Big 10 tournament and then rolled into the second weekend.AdvertisementMore: March Madness printable bracket 2026: Download NCAA Tournament bracketTramon Mark #12 of the Texas Longhorns attempts a shot while being guarded by Tyon Grant-Foster #7 and Davis Fogle #4 of the Gonzaga Bulldogs during the second half in the second round of the 2026 NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament at Moda Center on March 21, 2026 in Portland, Oregon.The Boilermakers are solid favorites, as the winner gets either Arizona or Arkansas in the Elite 8.Texas Longhorns men's basketball game todayThe No. 11 Texas men's basketball team takes on No. 2 Purdue in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA tournament's West Region in San Jose. The 5:10 p.m. MT/6:10 p.m. CT tip Thursday, March 26, will be aired on CBS.How to watch Texas vs. Purdue in the NCAA tournament Sweet 16The Texas vs. Purdue game will air on CBS at 5:10 p.m. MT/6:10 p.m. CT on Thursday, March 26.More: Predicting every Men's NCAA tournament game using AIAdvertisementWho does the winner of Texas-Purdue play?The winner of No. 11 Texas vs. No. 2 Purdue advances to the Elite 8 West Region final in San Jose, where it will play the winner of No. 1 Arizona vs. No. 4 Arkansas on Saturday.The Texas Longhorns are 21-14.More: USA Today NCAA basketball coveragePurdue men's basketball recordThe Purdue Boilermakers are 29-8.Texas Longhorns vs. Purdue Boilermakers oddsOdds from BetMGM.com: Purdue -7 1/2. Moneyline: Purdue -375, Texas +290. Over/under 147 1/2.Texas Longhorns men's basketball vs. Purdue Boilermakers predictions, picksThe Arizona Republic: Purdue 80, Texas 70Jeremy Cluff writes: \"We didn't have Texas making it past BYU in the first round, so we are very surprised the Longhorns are in the Sweet 16. An upset over Purdue for Sean Miller's team would be extremely surprising for us. The Boilermakers are tough.\"AdvertisementDimers: Purdue 80, Texas 71It writes: \"After extensive simulations, our model gives Texas a win probability of 22%, while Purdue has a win probability of 78%.\"ESPN: Purdue has a 75.5% chance to beat TexasThe site gives the Longhorns a 24.4% shot at defeating the Boilermakers in the NCAA Tournament March Madness Sweet 16 game.Bookies.com: Bet Purdue to cover vs TexasBill Speros writes: \"Another Big Ten-SEC Sweet 16 matchup - along with Michigan vs Alabama. In the West, Cinderella swapped those glass slippers for a pair of longhorns. Camden Heide hit a 3-pointer with 14.7 seconds left — his first points of the entire 2026 tournament — to seal Texas' upset of Gonzaga. Texas previously beat NC State (First Four) and BYU in reaching the Sweet 16. Purdue's run, meanwhile, has been steady and dominant. Purdue doesn't turn the ball over and Texas struggled to force them. Shop around as this number is floating between 7.5 and 8.5. This will be Texas' fifth game in 12 days. That's a big ask against a deep, physical and punishing Boilermakers' team. A close game opens up in the final 10 minutes.\"AdvertisementTopeka Capital-Journal: Take Purdue to beat TexasWyatt D. Wheeler writes: \"Texas isn't the most attractive Cinderella story we've ever seen. Purdue guard Braden Smith deserves some time in the spotlight.\"USA TODAY Sports: Go with Purdue to advance past TexasEight of nine experts on the site predict that Purdue will win the Sweet 16 game against Texas.Bret Bloomquist can be reached at bbloomquist@elpasotimes.com; @Bretbloomquist on X.This article originally appeared on El Paso Times: Texas Longhorns men's basketball vs. Purdue: TV, odds, predictions",
